            <ArticleTitle>Coronary artery bypass in a patient with single anomalous right coronary artery.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>577-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1177/0218492309343726</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The true incidence of coronary artery anomalies in the general population is unknown. Rarely, atherosclerotic coronary artery disease can be associated with single coronary artery. We describe coronary artery bypass surgery in a 57-year-old man with this association.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
